   "createTime": 1790658343,
   "desc": "If you’re planning 14 days in Vietnam around the end of the year, this route gives you a little bit of everything 🇻🇳✨ From the charm of Hanoi and misty mountains in Sapa to the dramatic landscapes of Ha Giang, vibrant Ho Chi Minh City, the Mekong Delta, and tropical beaches in Phu Quoc 🌿🏔️🌴 Here’s how I’d split the 14 days: 🏙️ Hanoi (2 days) 🌾 Sapa (2 days) ⛰️ Ninh Binh (1 day) 🏍️ Ha Giang (2 days) 🌆 Ho Chi Minh City (2 days) 🚤 Mekong Delta (1 day) 🏝️ Phu Quoc (4 days) A few tips for planning 👇 🚆 Start in Hanoi and spend your first two days exploring the Old Quarter, Train Street, Hoan Kiem Lake and some of the city’s best food spots. 🏔️ Head north to Sapa for mountain views, rice terraces and local villages. Then continue to Ninh Binh for limestone landscapes, rivers and ancient temples. 🏍️ Spend 2 days in Ha Giang for the famous Ha Giang Loop and spectacular mountain scenery. If you’re not comfortable riding yourself, you can also do the loop with an easy rider. ✈️ Fly south to Ho Chi Minh City and spend two days discovering the city before taking a day trip to the Mekong Delta for a completely different side of Vietnam. 🏝️ Finish your trip in Phu Quoc with four days of beaches, island-hopping, sunsets and a slower tropical escape. 🏨 You can keep the route simple with one main base in each destination, while Ha Giang and the Mekong Delta work better as dedicated overnight/day-trip experiences depending on your travel style. 📌 Save this 14-day Vietnam itinerary for your end-of-year trip! 🇻🇳✨ #VietnamTravel #VietnamTrip #VietnamItinerary #visitvietnam ",
